   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"7\">\n    <li>Below is a scatter plot of the data with two linear models, <span data-math=\"y=130-5x\">y=130-5x</span> and <span data-math=\"y=25.3+3.66x\">y=25.3+3.66x</span>. Which of these two models does a better job of describing how shoe length <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> and height <span data-math=\"y\">y</span> (in inches) are related?</li>\n  </ol>\n  <p><img alt=\"A SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS SHOE LENGTH ON THE X-AXIS AND HEIGHT ON THE Y-AXIS. TWO DIFFERENT LINEAR MODELS ARE SHOWN, ONE WITH A POSITIVE SLOPE AND ONE WITH A NEGATIVE SLOPE.  \" height=\"409\" src=\"exercises/media/86e3b840e95eef53.jpg\" width=\"450\"></p>",
